1. You are asked to create a docker image and you are trying to deploy the image to a web app as a container. but while you are build ing the docker image you are downloading the dependencies from jfrog artifactory. As you need to download the dependencies you need to configure the auth and authorization to jfrog. So how can you build a image without revealing the secrets


  You’re right to worry—ARG/ENV in a Dockerfile leak into image history. Use one of these safe patterns so creds never land in a layer:

1) BuildKit secrets (best) — no creds in layers/logs

Prereqs: Build with BuildKit (DOCKER_BUILDKIT=1), and Dockerfile syntax v1.4+.

Dockerfile

# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1.7
FROM python:3.11-slim AS builder
WORKDIR /app

# Only copy lockfiles first for better layer caching
COPY requirements.txt .

# Use a temp secret file during this RUN only (not stored in a layer)
RUN --mount=type=secret,id=pip_index_url \
    PIP_INDEX_URL="$(cat /run/secrets/pip_index_url)" \
    pip wheel --no-cache-dir --wheel-dir=/wheels -r requirements.txt

FROM python:3.11-slim
WORKDIR /app
# Copy prebuilt wheels (no secrets)
COPY --from=builder /wheels /wheels
COPY . .
RUN pip install --no-index --find-links=/wheels -r requirements.txt

CMD ["gunicorn","--bind","0.0.0.0:8000","app:app"]

Build command

# Example: pass secret via env var (from your CI secret store or Key Vault task)
DOCKER_BUILDKIT=1 docker buildx build \
  --secret id=pip_index_url,env=PIP_INDEX_URL \
  -t myorg/myapp:latest .

Why it’s safe
	•	The token is exposed only to that RUN step via /run/secrets/....
	•	It never appears in image layers or docker history.
	•	Nothing is printed unless you echo it.

⸻

2) pip.conf as a secret (clean & readable)

Put your authenticated repo in a temp pip.conf that exists only during the layer.

pip.conf (example)

[global]
index-url = https://<user-or-_token_>:<access-token>@<your-jfrog-host>/api/pypi/<repo>/simple
trusted-host = <your-jfrog-host>

Dockerfile

# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1.7
FROM python:3.11-slim AS builder
WORKDIR /app
COPY requirements.txt .

RUN --mount=type=secret,id=pip_conf,target=/etc/pip.conf \
    pip wheel --no-cache-dir --wheel-dir=/wheels -r requirements.txt

FROM python:3.11-slim
WORKDIR /app
COPY --from=builder /wheels /wheels
COPY . .
RUN pip install --no-index --find-links=/wheels -r requirements.txt
CMD ["gunicorn","--bind","0.0.0.0:8000","app:app"]

Build

DOCKER_BUILDKIT=1 docker buildx build \
  --secret id=pip_conf,src=./pip.conf \
  -t myorg/myapp:latest .


